Hi All,

We are working on adding Tru64 support to our Alpha emulator (see 
www.emulatorsinternationa.com). The emulated Alpha system is EB164.

The installation process sometimes succeeds for versions 4.0x and 5.1B 
(2650). If so, the system seems to be usable and operate correctly.

However sometimes the installer for 4.0x versions hangs after displaying 
the message "Initializing system for Digital UNIX installation.  Please 
wait...".

Tracing of the installation script shows that the problem is around the 
second call to mfs (mouning of the /dev file system).

The 5.1B installer sometimes fails with:
	dn_setup -install
	dn_setup: ERROR=30 - ignored.
It seems to happens soon after to the same mfs call. Sometimes it asks:
	override mode 755 on /dev/MAKEDEV?
	override mode 755 on /dev/SYSV_PTY?
	...
and fails to do so because the file system is readonly. Again, something 
goes wrong in mounting the dev file system here.

Have similar problems ever been experienced on real Alpha machines. I 
would appreciate any information that can shread some light on these 
problems.

Artem Alimarine
Software Architect,
Emulators International BV.
http://www.emulatorsinternationa.com


